Executives raised the company&#8217;s full-year 2026 guidance by $25 million each for revenue, adjusted EBITDA, and free cash flow to about&nbsp;$8.525 billion, $2.625 billion and $1.375 billion, respectively.

Here are the highlights:

- Second quarter revenue rose 1% year over year to&nbsp;$2.16 billion.&nbsp;

- Net income rose&nbsp;17% to $239 million, and diluted earnings per share were up 23% to $0.70.&nbsp;

- Adjusted EBITDA grew 3% to $691 million, with adjusted EBITDA margin expanding one percentage point to 32%.

- Free cash flow increased&nbsp;48% to $593 million.&nbsp;

- SiriusXM recorded&nbsp;22,000 self-pay net additions, its first positive second-quarter result in four years, supported by a&nbsp;record-low self-pay churn rate of 1.4%.&nbsp;

- SiriusXM raised its full-year revenue, adjusted EBITDA and free cash flow guidance by $25 million each, to approximately $8.525 billion, $2.625 billion and $1.375 billion, respectively.

- Companion subscriptions contributed&nbsp;123,000 incremental self-pay net additions&nbsp;during the quarter, alongside continued benefits from the company’s continuous service initiative and automotive dealer extended-duration plans.&nbsp;

- Sirius XM advertising revenue increased 8% overall to $454 million.
